Changes relative to upstream (required by LGPL 2.1 §2a — the full list is in the git history):
  - 2026-06-10: selective import of modules (cldc, midp, javase, javase-swing,
    nokiaui, siemensapi); NOT carried over: applet, SWT, webstart, android, iphone,
    device skins, JSR-75/120/82, JSR-135 (MMAPI), examples, tests,
    the Maven build, microemu-injected (a duplicate of org.microemu.Injected).
  - 2026-06-10: the 5 fixes from nikita36078/microemu applied (list above).
  - 2026-06-10: the build replaced with the javac script build.sh (JDK 17, --release 8).
  - 2026-06-10: a headless rendering smoke test added (smoke/).
  - 2026-06-10: ASM upgraded 3.1 -> 9.8; org.microemu.app.classloader
    (ChangeCallsClassVisitor, ChangeCallsMethodVisitor) ported to the ASM 9 API
    (ClassAdapter/MethodAdapter -> ClassVisitor/MethodVisitor(ASM9),
    visitMethodInsn with the isInterface flag) — instrumentation also works on
    modern bytecode (class file major 52+).
  - 2026-06-10: the CLI flag --no-instrument added (org.microemu.app.Common) —
    explicitly disables ASM instrumentation of MIDlet classes.
  - 2026-06-10: a minimal API stub layer for JSR-135 (MMAPI) added:
    javax.microedition.media[.control] (Manager, Player, Controllable, Control,
    PlayerListener, TimeBase, MediaException, VolumeControl, ToneControl) and
    org.microemu.media.NoopPlayer — written from the public JSR-135 specification
    for the fork (no sound is played; games using MMAPI load instead of failing with
    NoClassDefFoundError while resolving classes).
  - 2026-06-12: the JSR-135 layer extended to real sound: org.microemu.media.
    AbstractPlayer (state machine + event listeners + VolumeControl),
    MidiPlayer (javax.sound.midi, volume by intercepting CC7), SampledPlayer
    (javax.sound.sampled, WAV/AU/AIFF, MASTER_GAIN volume), ToneGenerator
    (Manager.playTone on top of javax.sound.midi); Manager dispatches by
    content-type/data signature (MThd/RIFF/.snd/FORM), unsupported
    formats still get NoopPlayer; the system property
    org.microemu.media.noop=true turns sound off (headless — by default).
  - 2026-06-10: org.microemu.app.Common — NPE guards when creating the
    MIDlet fails (loadMidlet == null no longer crashes initMIDlet/runAutoTests).
  - 2026-06-10: headless rendering of GameCanvas games: the interface
    org.microemu.device.j2se.J2SEGraphicsSurfaceDisplayComponent introduced
    (implemented by SwingDisplayComponent and NoUiDisplayComponent); J2SEDeviceDisplay.flushGraphics
    no longer hard-casts to SwingDisplayComponent (in headless that cast
    silently killed the game thread with a ClassCastException — the frames of GameCanvas games
    never reached the listener).
  - 2026-11-14: deterministic tick-based input (headless --ticks N):
    org.microemu.TickInput (frame boundary in Display.paint and
    J2SEDeviceDisplay.flushGraphics), org.microemu.app.headless.TickDriver;
    while a tick event is being delivered, keys/commands run synchronously and
    repaint() is not queued; a "tick" field in the --inputs scenario;
    flushGraphics writes the frame boundary "F n" into the trace; in tick mode "F n"
    has no wall time; ChoiceGroup's internal images are created bypassing
    Image.createImage and do not get into the trace.
  - 2026-11-15: --resizableDevice W H also sets the Canvas area, not only
    the full screen (Common.setDisplaySize, shared with Main.setDeviceSize): a normal
    Canvas gets W x (H - the soft-key bar), a fullscreen one W x H (it used to be
    176x176 from resizable/device.xml for any W x H); Canvas.setFullScreenMode
    resets the remembered size for any Canvas, not only for GameCanvas;
    the internal RMS record count (RecordEnumerationImpl.rebuild — enumerating
    and saving the store) bypasses the trace, only
    RecordStore.getNumRecords called by the game goes into the trace.
  - 2026-06-10: upstream files that came without license headers were given
    headers in line with the upstream licensing (COPYING), with a note about the fork.

